From 5147f70710a6aec99fc19137b97e01b4574ebe22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:36:11 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 105/106] Android: touch controls over menus, L2/R2 and
 two-button moves, a JNI-free data folder

- The on-screen controls stay over the game's dialogs and the port's panels
  (set_touch_for_interface); there they press ImGui's gamepad keys, and a
  tap off a control reaches the screen as before.
- L2 and R2 beside L and R, for a game that reads the extra buttons.
- A button for each of the game's moves made from two buttons together
  (GameProfile::combos), in two rows to the left of the face buttons.
- user_data_directory() on Android without JNI, so it works from static
  initialisers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
